{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgQ3UGLQY2GRGMZpCNWwb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I can't say whether Shift4 (FOUR) beat or missed. These tools couldn't get me the Q3 2024 end-to-end payment volume guidance from Q1 2024, or the actual Q3 2024 figure, so I can't work out a beat or miss percentage.\n\n**What I found:**\n- Shift4's Q1 2024 shareholder letter is Exhibit 99.1 to the 8-K filed 2024-05-09. A search for the phrases \"Q3 2024\" and \"payment volume\" together returns that letter, so it probably gives a Q3 2024 volume outlook.\n- The actual Q3 2024 result would be in the Q3 2024 shareholder letter (Exhibit 99.1 to the 8-K filed 2024-11-12), which mentions \"end-to-end payment volume\".\n\n**What's missing:**\n- The search tool only says which filings contain a phrase. It doesn't return the text, so I couldn't see the guidance range, its midpoint or the actual Q3 volume.\n- End-to-end payment volume is a non-GAAP measure that Shift4 doesn't tag in XBRL, so the financial-data tools don't have it either.\n- I didn't try guessing numbers in searches, because that could produce a false match.\n\nTo get the answer, open the two exhibits below. Take the midpoint of the Q3 2024 guidance range from the first, the actual Q3 volume from the second, and calculate (actual − midpoint) ÷ midpoint.\n\n**Sources**\n- Shift4 Payments 8-K, filed 2024-05-09, accession 0001794669-24-000014 (Ex. 99.1, Q1 2024 shareholder letter)\n- Shift4 Payments 8-K, filed 2024-08-08, accession 0001794669-24-000023 (Ex. 99.1, Q2 2024 shareholder letter)\n- Shift4 Payments 8-K, filed 2024-11-12, accession 0001794669-24-000031 (Ex. 99.1, Q3 2024 shareholder letter)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":714,"cache_read_input_tokens":7564,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":714},"outp